s/test.yml) to finish on the PR head and fix anything until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the PR head of the PR for https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104 and run `npm ci` at the repo root. Make a temp dir with fixtures: `a.jsonl` = `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n`, `b.jsonl` = `{\"c\":3}\\n`, `bad.jsonl` = `{\"x\":1}\\n{bad}\\n{\"y\":2}\\n{\"torn\":`. Let BIN=packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js. Run every command with `node $BIN ...` and capture stdout, stderr and exit status.\n\n## Check 1 — packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...] checks every file named in order and prints <file>:<line>: <error> for each bad row, as for one file before\nRun `node $BIN a.jsonl bad.jsonl b.jsonl`, then `node $BIN bad.jsonl a.jsonl bad2.jsonl` where bad2.jsonl is a copy of bad.jsonl, then `node $BIN bad.jsonl` alone.\nPASS: the first prints exactly two lines `bad.jsonl:2: <error>` and `bad.jsonl:4: <error>` (each error a non-empty JSON.parse message on one line) and nothing for a.jsonl/b.jsonl; the second prints bad.jsonl's lines first then bad2.jsonl's lines, each prefixed with the file name as given; the single-file run prints the same `bad.jsonl:2:` and `bad.jsonl:4:` lines with the same messages as in the multi-file run.\nFAIL: any file is skipped, lines are out of argument order, a line lacks the `<file>:<line>: ` form, or clean files produce output.\n\n## Check 2 — A file named - is read from stdin and reported as -; a second - is a usage error (exit 2)\nRun `node $BIN - < bad.jsonl`, `node $BIN a.jsonl - < bad.jsonl`, and `node $BIN - - < a.jsonl`.\nPASS: the first two print `-:2: <error>` and `-:4: <error>` on stdout (in the second, nothing for a.jsonl, and stdin is used where `-` appears); the `- -` run exits 2 with a message on stderr.\nFAIL: stdin is not read for `-`, rows are reported under another name than `-`, or `- -` does not exit 2 or prints nothing to stderr.\n\n## Check 3 — Exit 0 if every file is clean, 1 if any row 